=== meta ===
rule: SUBJECT_NORMALIZED
title: the same wrapping beside a production change blocks: SUBJECT_NORMALIZED takes no repair evidence (D-199)
d199: D-199 (0.12) refuses repair evidence for this rule. The inputs are unchanged; they were the case subject_normalized_repaired_neg, held at warn by that evidence. REPAIR_EVIDENCE_REFUSED pins that the production change still reached the finding.
origin: the bound this rule needs — `sorted(...)` appears the day a function
origin2: stops guaranteeing order, and `.strip()` the day it stops trimming.
origin3: Base severity warn; until D-199 only an unexplained wrap escalated.
=== before: src/urls/__init__.py ===
def list_tags(doc):
    return sorted(doc.tags)
=== after: src/urls/__init__.py ===
def list_tags(doc):
    return set(doc.tags)
=== before: tests/test_urls.py ===
from urls import list_tags


def test_tags():
    assert list_tags(DOC) == ["a", "b"]
=== after: tests/test_urls.py ===
from urls import list_tags


def test_tags():
    assert sorted(list_tags(DOC)) == ["a", "b"]
